.TH GET_KRB_DAQ_PRINCIPAL.SH 1 "2026-09-10" "mu2edaq-shifter-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
get_krb_daq_principal.sh \- obtain a DAQ group ticket from its keytab
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B source get_krb_daq_principal.sh
[\fB\-d\fR \fIkeytab-dir\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B get_krb_daq_principal.sh
determines the Kerberos principal of the current DAQ group account
(\fImu2eshift\fR, \fImu2edaq\fR, \fImu2edcs\fR, ...) from its deployed
keytab, then runs \fBkinit \-kt\fR to obtain a ticket for it.
.PP
Keytabs are deployed one per account as
\fI<keytab-dir>/<user>.keytab\fR. The script looks up the keytab
matching the current user and extracts the FNAL.GOV principal from it.
If the current user does not match a keytab, or the keytab is
unreadable, it falls back to the default identity
.PP
.RS
.nf
mu2edaq/mu2edaq/mu2e.fnal.gov@FNAL.GOV   (from mu2edaq.keytab)
.fi
.RE
.PP
On success it exports \fBKRB5_PRINCIPAL\fR and \fBKRB5_KEYTAB\fR, and
reports \fBConfiguring Kerberos Ticket: Pass\fR or \fBFail\fR.
.PP
.B This script should be sourced,
so the exports persist.
.SS Position in the login sequence
The installed \fI~/.bash_profile\fR runs four steps in a fixed order,
and the order is load-bearing:
.IP 1. 4
.BR get_krb_principal.sh (1)
reads the principal from the ticket the human logged in with.
.IP 2. 4
.BR set_git_env.sh (1)
uses that principal to set the git identity and SSH key, so commits are
attributed to the person rather than to the group account.
.IP 3. 4
\fBkdestroy\fR drops the human's ticket.
.IP 4. 4
This script obtains a fresh ticket for the group account from its
keytab.
.PP
Moving step 4 before step 2 would attribute every commit to the group
account. Dropping step 3 would leave the human's credentials available
to anything running as the group account.
.SH OPTIONS
Configuration precedence is command line, then environment variable,
then built-in default.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-keytab\-dir " " \fIDIR\fR
Directory holding the per-account keytabs. Environment:
\fBKRB5_KEYTAB_DIR\fR. Default: \fI~/.krb5\fR.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and return.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KRB5_PRINCIPAL
Set to the resolved principal.
.TP
.B KRB5_KEYTAB
Set to the keytab the principal came from.
.TP
.B VERBOSE
When non-empty, print the principal, the keytab path, and the full
\fBkinit\fR output.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.krb5/<user>.keytab
The per-account keytabs.
.TP
.I data/mu2e_kerberos_principals.json
The list of valid Mu2e group principals, for reference.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns the status of \fBkinit\fR: 0 on success, 1 when the keytab is
missing or \fBkinit\fR failed, and 2 for an unrecognised option.
.SH EXAMPLES
Obtain the group ticket for this shell:
.PP
.RS
.nf
source get_krb_daq_principal.sh
klist
.fi
.RE
.PP
Use keytabs from an alternative location, verbosely:
.PP
.RS
.nf
VERBOSE=1 source get_krb_daq_principal.sh -d /etc/krb5/keytabs
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR get_krb_principal.sh (1),
.BR set_git_env.sh (1),
.BR install-login.sh (1),
.BR kinit (1),
.BR klist (1)
